===Etymology===
From classical {{etyl|la}} {{m|la|solidus||[[solid]]}}. ''See'' '''[[solid]]'''. In [[numismatic]] and weight senses, via medieval {{etyl|la}} {{m|la|solidus||[[various]] [[coin]]s}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|solidus||a [[gold coin]] of the [[Roman Empire]]}}. In chemical sense, via {{etyl|de}} {{term|Solidus|lang=de}}, coined by [[w:H.W.B. Roozeboom|H.W.B. Roozeboom]] in his 1899 ''Zeitschrift für Physikalische Chemie, Stöchiometrie, und Verwandtschaftslehre'' (XXX, p. 387).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɒlɪdəs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|solidi|soliduses}}

# {{context|historical|lang=en}} [[various|Various]] [[medieval]] and [[early]] [[modern]] [[coin]]s or [[units of account]], ''[[particular]]ly:''
## A [[Roman]] ~23[[carat|k]] [[gold coin]] [[introduce]]d by [[Diocletian]] in <small>[[AD]]</small>&nbsp;301.
## Its [[successor]] [[Byzantine]] [[gold coin|coin]]s, of [[progressive]]ly [[debase]]d [[weight]] and [[purity]].
## {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} {{altname|sol|lang=en|nodot=1}} or [[sou]]: a [[Carolingian]] [[unit of account]] [[equivalent]] to a {{l|en|solidus|id=French weight}} of [[silver]].
## {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} {{altname|soldo|lang=en|nodot=1}}: the [[silver]] [[coin]]s of [[various]] [[Italian]] [[state]]s.
## {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} {{altname|shilling|lang=en|nodot=1}}: an [[English]] [[unit of account]] and, [[follow]]ing the [[Tudor]] [[dynasty]], [[silver]] [[coin]].
# {{context|historical|lang=en}} The [[weight]] of the [[Roman]] [[gold coin]], 1/60 of a [[Roman pound]] under [[Diocletian]] or 1/72 [[lb]]. (about 4.5 [[gram]]s) after [[Constantine]].
# {{senseid|en|French weight}} {{context|historical|lang=en}} A [[medieval]] [[French]] [[weight]], 1/20 of the [[Carolingian]] [[pound]].
# {{context|typography|lang=en}} {{altname|slash|lang=en|nodot=1}} ⟨'''[[/]]'''⟩, [[originally]] {{context|UK|lang=en}} in [[its]] [[use]] as the [[shilling mark]] and [[now]] [[its]] [[formal]] [[designation]] by the [[ISO]] and [[Unicode]].
# {{context|typography|lang=en}} The [[formal]] [[name]] of the [[oblique]] [[strikethrough]] [[overlay]] (as in A̷ and B̸) in [[Unicode]].
# {{context|typography|lang=en}} The [[division]] [[line]] between the [[numerator]] and the [[denominator]] of a [[fraction]], [[whether]] [[horizontal]] or [[oblique]].
# {{label|en|chemistry|physics}} The [[line]] in a [[phase diagram]] [[mark]]ing the [[temperature]]s and [[pressure]]s below which a [[given]] [[substance]] is a [[stable]] [[solid]].
